  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 408.03 Aggregation of Projects: Consistent Scheme of Development",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 408.03 Aggregation of Projects: Consistent Scheme of Development.\n\n(a) As authorized by RSA 482-A:11, V, a series of minor or minimum impact projects, or any combination thereof, undertaken by a single developer or several developers within the 5 years preceding the application for the current project shall constitute a major impact project if the projects, when taken in the aggregate, meet any of the criteria for a major impact project as identified in Env-Wt 407.02 or Env-Wt 407.03, and:\n\n(1) The subject properties are abutting;\n\n(2) The projects are a part of an overall scheme of development; or\n\n(3) The projects are otherwise consistent parts of an eventual whole.\n\n(b) Classification as a major impact project based on (a), above, shall:\n\n(1) Take precedence over any lower classification; and\n\n(2) Not be eligible for a waiver or downgrade of the classification.\n\nSource. #12804, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt400.html"
